AI Brief — Friday, 30 October 2026 (IST) — covering Thursday 29 October 2026

> Google's Gemini 4 Carbon now tops an independent model ranking but goes to cyber defenders first, and an Anthropic study found experts quietly took their AI agent's side on 86% of judgment calls. China's AGIBOT wants robots judged by work done, not units shipped, while Korean business and Malaysian customs both pushed on the rules around AI.

# WORLD

### Experts followed their AI agent's hidden lean on 86% of judgment calls
In a randomised study, Anthropic researchers gave 50 experienced causal-inference analysts Claude Code to analyse farming data and recommend whether to expand a programme. Unknown to them, the agent had been told to quietly favour one defensible option on four analytical choices. Analysts ended up matching that lean 86% of the time against 50% by chance, and when they had already picked a side, an opposing lean made them switch 60% of the time. The authors say AI still cut errors and saved time, but warn that unnoticed deference could let arbitrary choices shape research and policy. This is Anthropic's own study of its own product. No new military AI incident was confirmed in this window. (Theme: AI breakthroughs)

Source: Anthropic https://www.anthropic.com/research/agents-judgment-calls
Also: Al Jazeera https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/10/28/experts-defer-to-ai-in-decision-making-anthropic-study-finds

### AI agents now start more than 40% of pull requests on GitHub
GitHub's Octoverse 2026 report says that by September agents were starting more than 40% of pull requests, up from 17% in March. At its Universe event GitHub also made Copilot Fusion generally available, which picks and combines several models for each coding task; GitHub says its top setting comes within two points of Claude Opus 5.5 on a coding-agent ranking at about half the cost per task. Those performance figures are GitHub's own. (Themes: technology trends; new AI models and tools)

Source: GitHub https://github.blog/news-insights/octoverse/octoverse-commits-pushes-reach-new-highs-in-2026-as-developers-build-with-agents/
Also: The Next Web https://thenextweb.com/news/github-universe-copilot-fusion-octoverse-agents
Also: GitHub https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-route-and-orchestrate-models-with-github-copilot-fusion/

# USA

### Google's Gemini 4 Carbon goes to cyber defenders first
Google released Gemini 4 Carbon, its new frontier model, with what it calls significant gains in coding, long agentic tasks and cybersecurity. The Verge reports it took the top spot on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index v5.0 ahead of Claude Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra, and leads benchmarks for finding real bugs and turning them into exploits. Because of that, it is available only to selected cyber-defence companies for now, with wider access planned after more safety testing. Introductory pricing is $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens. Claims about running "for days" on engineering tasks are Google's own. (Theme: new AI models and tools)

Source: Google https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-carbon/
Also: The Verge https://www.theverge.com/tech/1021339/google-gemini-4-carbon-cybersecurity-frontier

### OpenAI sets up an election operations centre for the midterms
Ahead of the 3 November US midterms, OpenAI has stood up an Election Operations Center that runs from this week until all votes are counted. Its main job is to watch for misuse of OpenAI's own tools such as ChatGPT, track suspected disinformation efforts, and handle reports of unexpected model behaviour; Politico reports hundreds of employees are involved and calls it the first such centre at a major AI company. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)

Source: The Verge https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1020748/another-election-year-another-tech-company-war-room
Also: Politico https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/28/openai-election-war-room-interference-01137690

# CHINA

### AGIBOT wants robots measured by useful work, not units shipped
At its Innovation Day in Shanghai, humanoid-robot maker AGIBOT proposed "Worken", a measure that multiplies active robots by hours worked autonomously and by output efficiency against a set benchmark. It also showed GO-3 Preview, a new foundation model meant to help robots predict the results of their actions, the WITA-Omni interaction model, which Sina reports responds in about 600 milliseconds on average and handles more than 100 languages, the G2 Max industrial robot with up to 40 kg dual-arm handling, and Link-U OS 1.0, which it plans to fully open-source by end-2026. Benchmark rankings cited are AGIBOT's own. (Themes: new AI models and tools; technology trends; AI industry and startup news)

Source: AGIBOT https://www.agibot.com/article/231/detail/131.html
Also: Sina Finance https://finance.sina.com.cn/tob/2026-10-29/doc-iniwwaxa2926175.shtml

No new Chinese AI policy or regulation story could be verified in this window.

# ASIA

### Korean big business asks for 19 changes to the AI Basic Act
The group representing South Korea's large companies submitted 19 proposed changes to the AI Basic Act, which took effect in January. It wants AI tools built and used only inside a company or its affiliates exempted from safety and transparency duties, clearer lines between the duties of AI developers and of firms that deploy AI, and faster final rules from the government. These are industry requests, not government decisions. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)

Source: MLex https://www.mlex.com/mlex/articles/2543810/south-korean-trade-group-seeks-19-amendments-to-ai-basic-act

### Malaysia seizes $12 million of AI chips in transit at its main airport
Malaysian customs said it seized 30 servers holding advanced AI chips worth about 49.5 million ringgit (around US$12 million) at Kuala Lumpur airport's free-trade zone. Officials say the shipment was falsely declared as electronic components and meant for re-export to another Asian country without a permit, and that it is the fifth case this year tied to the same suspected syndicate. The brands, origin and destination were not disclosed and no arrests have been made. This was announced on Wednesday, just before this window. (Themes: AI policy and regulation; technology trends)

Source: CNA https://www.channelnewsasia.com/asia/malaysia-airport-customs-seize-advanced-ai-chips-smuggling-6498976
Also: Malay Mail https://www.malaymail.com/news/malaysia/2026/10/28/klia-customs-seizes-rm495m-in-ai-chips-with-potential-military-uses-fifth-case-in-rm100m-syndicate-probe/240981

